Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:10:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] Blaze 3.x (Madden): heat2 getServerInstance + plaintext
 session -> reaches EA handshake

- Heat2Writer: a Blaze 3.x "heat2" wire encoder (3-byte tag + full type byte;
  little-endian varint ints, distinct from heat1's big-endian EncodeVlq).
- GetServerInstanceHandler: for BlazeSDK major>=3 (Madden 13.3, NHL), hand-build the
  getServerInstance response in heat2 (ADDR union case 0 -> VALU{IP,PORT}; SECU; XDNS);
  the 2.x model encoder produces heat1 the client can't parse.
- Run the Blaze SESSION in plaintext (SECU=0) on the normal port. A SECU=1 address
  given as a bare IP makes the client's ProtoSSL refuse to start TLS (no hostname/CN
  to validate) -> "EA servers not available". Plaintext avoids it and the client
  honours SECU=0. (env BLAZE3_SESSION=tls:<port>|plain:<port> keeps the toggle.)

Verified 2026-11-07: Madden reaches the redirector over TLS, connects the session
plaintext to 42100, sends preAuth (Util 0x07) + fetchClientConfig (OSDK_*), and the
UI shows "uscltest is connecting to the EA Servers". Remaining: a heat2 codec for the
session commands (the server still answers in heat1, so it stalls mid-handshake).
